            <ArticleTitle>A sticky situation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>491-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 19-year-old woman presented with frontal headaches, papilledema, and binocular horizontal double vision due to a left VI nerve palsy. MRV demonstrated sagittal sinus and bilateral transverse sinus thrombosis. The clinical and neuro-radiologic signs resolved after anticoagulation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
